`max_connections` is 30 and a `reporting` dashboard has opened 30 connections that sit idle (`Sleep`).
Root still gets in through the one reserved admin slot.

```sql
SELECT user, COUNT(*) FROM information_schema.processlist GROUP BY user;
-- kill them all in one go:
SELECT GROUP_CONCAT(CONCAT('KILL ', id, ';') SEPARATOR ' ') FROM information_schema.processlist WHERE user = 'reporting';
-- (paste the output) or per id: KILL 42;
ALTER USER 'reporting'@'localhost' WITH MAX_USER_CONNECTIONS 5;
```
Worth doing too: a lower `wait_timeout` so idle connections get closed, and a connection pool (or ProxySQL)
in front of chatty clients.

**Lesson:** the reserved admin connection is your way in when everything else is locked out, so don't give
`CONNECTION_ADMIN` to apps. Per-account limits (`MAX_USER_CONNECTIONS`) stop one client starving the rest.

```js
use app
const dups = db.users.aggregate([
  { $sort: { updatedAt: -1 } },
  { $group: { _id: { $toLower: "$email" }, ids: { $push: "$_id" }, n: { $sum: 1 } } },
  { $match: { n: { $gt: 1 } } }
]).toArray();
let gone = 0;
dups.forEach(d => gone += db.users.deleteMany({ _id: { $in: d.ids.slice(1) } }).deletedCount);
gone

// Option A: unique, case-insensitive index (collation strength 2 ignores case)
db.users.createIndex({ email: 1 }, { unique: true, collation: { locale: "en", strength: 2 } })
// Option B: normalise, then a plain unique index
// db.users.updateMany({}, [{ $set: { email: { $toLower: "$email" } } }]); db.users.createIndex({ email: 1 }, { unique: true })
```
**Lesson:** an application-level "check, then insert" is a race. Uniqueness belongs in the database, as an index.
Note that queries only use a collation index when they specify the same collation.
